  "adaptation": "Original arithmetic, float casts and execution order; explicit reward row, property dictionary and property parser boundaries. Original unsettled-preview argument order, truncation, fractional seconds and award clamp retained. Full original enums; selected prop_cfg flags. Offline checkpoint and award transactions remain separate.",
  "free_fast_forward_adapter": "Selected function 53 keyed by fast-hang-up ID, configured free count plus original non-battle property 1101, and read-only expired-count projection. User-confirmed local 06:00 day boundary reuses OfflineRefreshClock; old midnight-era morning counters migrate without granting another use.",
  "collection_adapter": "CollectReward projects only the committed claim delta, selected output item and durable ledger identity; presentation does not issue a second grant. Failed character experience mutations retain the local ledger; previously committed character receipts acknowledge without another award. The ledger persists a sealed transfer amount before granting; later same-item claims receive a separate serial until acknowledgement.",
  "ordinary_settlement_adapter": "User-confirmed ordinary claims follow the original client unsettled preview, independently of hourly/fast output argument order. Original fractional remainder is persisted when finite; pending local time and its subsecond checkpoint commit atomically with the claim. Failed grants retain the previous time, reward selection state and receipt.",
  "native_bed_adapter": "Complete selected FurnitureBedDialog prefab/controller, original output foldouts, quick-receive condition, property chunks and inventory response phases are bound to the actual local home/profile. No remote disable keys are installed, matching original empty-key HasKey=false. The original blessing-rule window uses selected rule_tip rows, actual blessing level, eleven original pooled rows and real home limits; its pointer, scrolling, highlight and mask-close behavior are covered. Secondary acceleration and activity-output details are not covered by this production-bed validation.",
